*9/16/86 Clean up the parsing of XFER'd files.                   [1.24]
*        This REVERSES the meaning of S#NXFER SITEOPT.           [1.24]
*        Add call to CNTRCVD to check hop count.                 [1.24]
*[1.23]Take Reg Quinton's mod for INCOMING table;  it now works  [1.23]
*      for a local user as well as from net. This mod is done    [1.23]
*      slightly differently from Reg's.                          [1.23]
*[1.22] Check for RSCS-domain as part of a valid host name       [1.22]
*[1.18] Added test for transferred files
*[1.16] Added support for Resent- fields.
*        also change AT to @
VALIDATE TITLE 'CUCCA VM NETWORK MAILER - VERSION 1 - MAIL FILE SENDER *
                VALIDATION'
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
*      MAILER -- Copyright (c) 1982,1985 Columbia University.         *
*    Program Property of the Trustees of Columbia University in the   *
*    City of New York.                                                *
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
VALIDATE CSECT ,
* VALIDATE -
*  Validate checks to see that the minimum required fields are
*  present in the message header.  These are "Date:" and
*  "From:" or "Sender:" and "From:".   In addition, it checks
*  that the following fields appear no more than once (other
*  fields may be repeated -- although it looks stupid):
*  "Date:", "From:", "Sender:", "Reply-to:" [RFC733 iii.c]
*  it also verifies that the sender of the mail file is
*  authorized to send mail and is not sending mail under an
*  assumed name.  this function is done differently depending
*  on the mail file source:
*        (1) File is from a local user (mflg1lcl is on).
*        the "Sender:", or "From:" field is checked to see if
*        the userid corresponds with the userid found in the
*        spool file block.
*        (2) File is from a network mailer (mflg1lcl is off).
*        the sending node name is looked up in the routing table.
*        the vm userid of the sending user (from rscs tag) must
*        correspond to the name of the mailer at that node. it
*        is assumed that that mailer has done validity checking
*        of mail that it is forwarding.
*        if the allow-unknown-nodes option is on, then unknown
*        network nodes can send files to mailer.  an optional
*        validity exit named *default* will be invoked for these
*        nodes if it is supplied.
*[1.16]  First check for RESENT- fields and do similar processing
*[1.16]  as above
*1.16    NOTE:  Although RFC822 states that multiple occurences of
*1.16    a RESENT field is undefined,  the DEC-20 implementation
*1.16    allows a file to be resent multiple times.  To handle this,
*1.16    only pay attention to the last "group" of resent fields
*1.16    where group "n" is defined by the Nth occurence of a
*1.16    resent-date.  It is considered an error to have more
*1.16    resent field repetitions than the number for the resent-date
*1.16    field.  (4 Resent-froms and 3 resent-dates is illegal while
*1.16    3 of each is legal.  And 3 froms and 4 dates is OK and means
*1.16    there is no resent-from field for the last resent group).
*  SPECIAL CASE:
*        If the file was generated by this mailer (i.e. userid *)
*        then it may be from one of three sources:
*          a) MAILRET is returning an error message.
*          b) RSCS rejected a file and transferred it back.
*          c) A user transferred a file back.
*        Case (a) can be checked since MAILRET sets the tag to
*        read "--- returned mail file ---".
*        Case (b) will contain the tag "<nodename> <userid>"
*        which Mailer just put into it when punching the file.
*        Case (c) should have no tag.  However the user may
*        tag the file prior to transferring it back.
*
*
* LAST EDIT: 5/23/82 BY ALAN CROSSWELL
*
* CALLED VIA - CALL VALIDATE,(MAILBLOK)
*    MAILBLOK=ADDRESS OF MAILBLOK MACRO EXPANSION
PAB      DSECT ,
@MBLOK   DS    A             ADDRESS OF MAILBLOK
         SPACE ,
*
         SPACE
* REGISTER USAGE -
R0  EQU  0 -
R1  EQU  1 -
R2  EQU  2 -
R3  EQU  3 -
R4  EQU  4 -
R5  EQU  5 -
R6  EQU  6 -
R7  EQU  7 -
R8  EQU  8 - VALD BASE
R9  EQU  9 - STACK POINTER
R10 EQU 10 - STACK LENGTH
R11 EQU 11 - MAILBLOK BASE
R12 EQU 12 - PROGRAM BASE
R13 EQU 13 - SAVE AREA
R14 EQU 14 - SUBROUTINE LINKAGE
R15 EQU 15 - SUBROUTINE LINKAGE
         SPACE
         PRINT NOGEN
         BLOCKS ,
         MAILBLOK ,
         EJECT
VALIDATE CSECT ,
         USING VALIDATE,R15  TEMPORARY ADDRESSABILITY
         B     EYESKIP       BRANCH OVER EYESKIP
MYNAME   DC    CL8'VALIDATE',CL8'&SYSDATE'
EYESKIP  DS    0H
         DROP  R15
         STM   R14,R12,12(R13) SAVE CALLER'S REGS
         LR    R12,R15       PERMANENT ADDRESSABILITY
         USING VALIDATE,R12
         LA    R14,SAVE      MY SAVE AREA
         ST    R13,4(R14)    SAVE CALLER'S PTR
         ST    R14,8(R13)    CHAIN MINE BACK
         LR    R13,R14       SET MY SAVE PTR
         USING PAB,R1        ADDRESS PARMS
         L     R11,@MBLOK    GET MAILBLOK BASE
         DROP  R1
         USING MAILBLOK,R11  GET MAILBLOK ADDRESSABILITY
         LM    R9,R10,STACKP GET STACK POINTERS
         NI    MAILFLG1,X'FF'-MFLG1RES [1.16]
         SPACE ,
***begin [1.18]------------------------------------------------------
*        Check if the file was transferred to me and disallow this
*        ONLY if the site options say so.
*[1.24] REVERSE meaning of S#NXFER.                              [1.24]
*--------------------------------------------------------------------
         TM    SITEOPTS,S#NXFER  ENABLE this checking selected?  [1.24]
         BZ    SKIPXFER      don't do the xfer check
         LA    R1,MAILSFB    get the sfblok
         USING SFBLOK,R1     address it
         TM    SFBFLAG3,SFBXFER  was it transferred?
         BO    BADXFER       kill this one.
         DROP  R1            done with SFBLOK
SKIPXFER EQU   *             here when xfer doesn't get checked
*end [1.18]----------------------------------------------------------
         SPACE ,
*--------------------------------------------------------------------
*  check the special case that the file is locally generated by
*  this mailer.  If it is,  it can have one of 3 tags/xfer status[1.24]
*            tag                       xfer status               [1.24]
*     ==========================       ==========================[1.24]
*  1) --- returned mail file ---       NOT xfer'd (direct from *)[1.24]
*  2) FILE (....) ORIGIN ...           xfer'd (from recipient)   [1.24]
*  3) nodename userid                  xfer'd (from RSCS)        [1.24]
*                                                                [1.24]
*  (1) means I am punching a file back to self for handling.     [1.24]
*  (2) means a (dumb) user transferred this file back to MAILER  [1.24]
*  (3) means RSCS transferred it back because the nodename       [1.24]
*      is not known by RSCS.                                     [1.24]
*  Note that (2) or (3) can be counterfeited by a recipient user [1.24]
*  who explicitly sets the TAG of the file and then transfers it [1.24]
*  back to mailer.  Hence,  the more paranoid S#NXFER option.    [1.24]
*--------------------------------------------------------------------
         TM    MAILFLG1,MFLG1LCL       IS IT LOCAL?
         BNO   NOTSPCL       NOT THE SPECIAL CASE
         CLC   MAILUSER,MAILVMID  FILE ORIG AND SELF THE SAME?
         BNE   NOTSPCL       NOT THE SPECIAL CASE
* (1) Check for XFER.  Should always fail for pre-SP2 CMS which  [1.24]
*     is OK.  We will just fall thru for pre-SP2 sites....       [1.24]
         LA    R1,MAILSFB    get the sfblok                      [1.24]
         USING SFBLOK,R1     addressability                      [1.24]
         TM    SFBFLAG3,SFBXFER  was it transferred?             [1.24]
         BO    SPCL2         -> yes, so it can't be case (1)     [1.24]
         DROP  R1            see if it is really case (1):       [1.24]
         CLC   =C'--- returned mail file ---',MAILTAG
         BE    NOTSPCL       -> In this case, I trust me.        [1.24]
SPCL2    EQU   *             <- XFER'd or drop down thru above.  [1.24]
* (2) Check for user XFER.                                       [1.24]
         CLC   =C'FILE (',MAILTAG  user xfer'd back?             [1.24]
         BE    BADUXFER      -> bad user xfer.  sigh.            [1.24]
* (3) ASSUME THE FILE WAS REJECTED BY RSCS                       [1.24]
         LA    R5,MAILTAG    ADDRESS OF NODENAME
         WTR   VAL036,(CA,(R5))   WRITE THE MESSAGE              [1.24]
         OI    MAILFLG1,MFLG1REJ SET REJECTION FLAG
NOTSPCL  EQU   *             END OF SPECIAL CASE
         SPACE ,
*----------------------------------------------------------------[1.24]
*  Count the number of "Received:" headers and fail if greater   [1.24]
*  than MAXRCVD.  If MAXRCVD == 0,  skip this check.             [1.24]
*----------------------------------------------------------------[1.24]
         CLC   MAXRCVD,=F'0' not doing hop count checks?         [1.24]
         BE    RCVDOK        -> skip hop count call              [1.24]
         CALL  CNTRCVD       count number of Received headers    [1.24]
         C     R15,MAXRCVD   retcode is number seen (or zero)    [1.24]
         BH    HOPCOUNT      -> hop max exceeded                 [1.24]
RCVDOK   EQU   *             <- here when hop count bypassed     [1.24]
*--------------------------------------------------------------------
*        CHECK FOR THE EXISTENCE OF THE REQUIRED FIELDS:
*        "DATE:", "FROM:" OR "FROM:" AND "SENDER:"
*--------------------------------------------------------------------
         SPACE ,
         XC    MAILDFLD,MAILDFLD [1.16]zero date ptr until we see it.
*[1.16]check for Resent-Date first.
         L     R5,MAILKTAB   get keyword table
         CALL  TBLUK,((R5),RDATE,L'RDATE,TWORK)
         LTR   R15,R15       find it?
         BNZ   CKDATE        check for just plain "date:"
         OI    MAILFLG1,MFLG1RES set resent- flag
*[1.16]RESENT-DATE found,  scan down FIEXTN's to find the latest
*[1.16] date of resending.
         USING FIELDD,R1     address the FIELDD
RCK#0    EQU   *
         CLC   FIEXTN,=F'0'  is this the last occurence of it?
         BE    RCK#1         out of loop
         ICM   R1,B'0111',FIEXTN chain along
         B     RCK#0         itterate the search
RCK#1    EQU   *             here when last extension found
         MVC   RESCNT,FIECNT [1.16]set count of # of resent groups
         DROP  R1            done with FIELDD
         B     GOODDATE      go back to old code now
CKDATE   EQU   *             [1.16]
**-- FIRST, CHECK FOR EXISTENCE OF 'DATE:'
         L     R5,MAILKTAB   GET KEYWORD TABLE
         CALL  TBLUK,((R5),DATE,L'DATE,TWORK)
         LTR   R15,R15       FIND ONE?
         BZ    GOODDATE
         TM    MAILOPTS,MOPTDEF        DO THEY WANT DEFAULT DATE
*                                     PROVIDED
         BNO   NODATE        SORRY, COMPLAIN ABOUT DATE MISSING
         TM    MAILFLG1,MFLG1LCL       AND IS THE FILE LOCAL?
         BNO   NODATE
         BAL   R14,FILLDATE  FILL THE DATE FIELD
GOODDATE EQU   *
         ST    R1,MAILDFLD   [1.16]save -> date fieldd
         LR    R6,R1         GET FIELDD POINTER
         USING FIELDD,R6     GET THE DATE FIELDD
         CLC   FIEXTN,=A(0)  ONLY ALLOW 1 OCCURENCE OF "DATE:"
         BNE   NODATE        SORRY.. YOU CAN'T GIVE 2 DATES...
         DROP  R6
         SPACE ,
*****************begin [1.16]*************************************
*[1.16]look for RESENT-SENDER first
         L     R5,MAILKTAB   address of keyword table
         CALL  TBLUK,((R5),RSENDER,L'RSENDER,TWORK)
         LTR   R15,R15       find it
         BZ    RSNDROK       RESENT-sender ok
*[1.16]look for RESENT-FROM if resent-sender not found
         L     R5,MAILKTAB   get the table
         CALL  TBLUK,((R5),RFROM,L'RFROM,TWORK)
         LTR   R15,R15       find it?
         BNZ   CKSEND        no RESENT-sender, try plain sender
RSNDROK  EQU   *             here when we've found a resent sender
         TM    MAILFLG1,MFLG1RES did we see a resent-date?
         BNO   NODATE        resent-from but no resent-date is bad
         USING FIELDD,R1     look at it
RS#0     EQU   *             loop to find last extension
         CLC   FIEXTN,=F'0'  is this the last extension
         BE    RS#1          out of loop
         ICM   R1,B'0111',FIEXTN  chain along
         B     RS#0          itterate
RS#1     EQU   *             here when last fieldd found
         CLC   RESCNT,FIECNT compare number of resent-dates seen to
*                            number of resent-froms seen.
         BH    NOSNDR        more dates than froms: No sender error
         BL    NODATE        more froms than dates: No date error
         B     SNDROK        sender is OK
         DROP  R1            done with FIELDD
CKSEND   EQU   *             [1.16]here for non-RESENT
         TM    MAILFLG1,MFLG1RES is resent-flag set?
         BO    NOSNDR        resent-date with no resent-from is bad
*********************end [1.16]*********************************
* - LOOK FOR "SENDER:" FIELD FIRST -
         L     R5,MAILKTAB   ADDRESS OF KEYWORD TABLE
         CALL  TBLUK,((R5),SENDER,L'SENDER,TWORK)
         LTR   R15,R15       FIND IT?
         BZ    SNDROK        YES, A SENDER FIELD WAS FOUND
* - LOOK FOR "FROM:" FIELD IF "SENDER:" ISN'T THERE -
         L     R5,MAILKTAB   ADDRESS OF KEYWORD TABLE
         CALL  TBLUK,((R5),FROM,L'FROM,TWORK)
         LTR   R15,R15       FIND IT?
         BZ    SNDROK        HAVE A SENDER, NOW CHECK IT
         TM    MAILOPTS,MOPTDEF        DEFAULT SENDER TO BE PROVIDED
         BNO   NOSNDR        NO SENDER OR DEFAULT PROVIDED...
         TM    MAILFLG1,MFLG1LCL       FOR A LOCAL USER
         BNO   NOSNDR
         SPACE ,
*--------------------------------------------------------------------
*  SUPPLY DEFAULT SENDER INFORMATION.
*--------------------------------------------------------------------
         BAL   R14,FILLSEND  FILL IN THE SENDER FIELD
SNDROK   EQU   *             R1 = FIELDD BASE
         ST    R1,MAILSFLD   SAVE IN MAILBLOK FOR FUTURE USE
         LR    R6,R1         GET FIELDD POINTER
         USING FIELDD,R6     ADDRESS IT
         CLC   FIEXTN,=A(0)  BETTER NOT BE ANY EXTENSIONS OF IT
         BNE   NOSNDR        SENDER IS NOT SO NICE
*----------------------------------------------------------------[1.23]
*        See if this is an RSCS reject (non-exist node)          [1.23]
*----------------------------------------------------------------[1.23]
         TM    MAILFLG1,MFLG1REJ FILE REJECTED BY RSCS?
         BO    RSCSREJ       JUST RETURN
*----------------------------------------------------------------[1.23]
*        Look the LOCAL or NETWORK sender up in the INCOMING     [1.23]
*        table before anything else.                             [1.23]
*----------------------------------------------------------------[1.23]
         MVC   NETNODE(8),MAILNODE    source node                [1.23]
         MVC   NETNODE+8(8),MAILUSER  source user                [1.23]
         L     R5,MAILVTAB            INCOMING table             [1.23]
         CALL  TBLUK,((R5),NETNODE,L'NETNODE,TWORK) look         [1.23]
         LR    R8,R1                  VALD ptr into R8           [1.23]
         LTR   R15,R15                was it found?              [1.23]
         BNZ   NOTHERE                nope                       [1.23]
         USING VALD,R8                look at the VALD           [1.23]
         ICM   R15,B'1111',VAADDR     user exit supplied?        [1.23]
         DROP  R8                     done w/vald                [1.23]
         BZ    VALTRUST               no; trust the sender       [1.23]
         ST    R11,USERVPAR           set up exit plist          [1.23]
         ST    R8,USERVPAR+4          "                          [1.23]
         LA    R1,USERVPAR            point to PLIST             [1.23]
         BALR  R14,R15                call it                    [1.23]
         LTR   R15,R15                did they like him?         [1.23]
         BNZ   VALFAIL                he's a bad guy.            [1.23]
         B     VALTRUST               he's a good guy.           [1.24]
*----------------------------------------------------------------[1.23]
*        Sender not in the table.  If a local user,  that's ok   [1.23]
*        as long as his address parses ok.  For remote senders,  [1.23]
*        it's OK only if MOPTAUN allows Unknown senders.         [1.23]
*----------------------------------------------------------------[1.23]
NOTHERE  EQU   *                                                 [1.23]
         TM    MAILFLG1,MFLG1LCL  LOCAL OR NETWORK SOURCE?
         BNO   NETWORK                from remote sender         [1.23]
         SPACE ,
*--------------------------------------------------------------------
*   FILE IS FROM A LOCAL USER.  VERIFY THAT THE SUPPLIED SENDER
*   AND THE SENDER IN THE SFBLOK ARE THE SAME USER.
*       ( R6->FIELDD )
*--------------------------------------------------------------------
LOCUSER  EQU   *
         L     R5,FIPARS     GET PARSE LIST
         USING MBOX,R5     ADDRESS THE ADDRESS DESCRIPTOR
         CLC   MBXNEXT,=A(0) BETTER NOT BE A LIST OF FROMS
         BNE   BADLOC
         CLC   MBXLCNT,=F'1' ONLY 1 TOKEN FOR USER NAME?
         BNE   BADLOC        NO, NOT A VM USERID...
         L     R7,MBXLCL         GET USER NAME NODE
         USING NODE,R7     ADDRESS IT
         L     R4,NODDOWN    GET POINTER TO TOKEND
         USING TOKEND,R4     GET TOKEN DESCRIPTOR
         DROP  R7
         SR    R7,R7         GET A ZERO
         L     R7,TOKLEN     GET LENGTH OF TOKEN
         L     R2,TOKPTR         GET ADDRESS OF STRING
         DROP  R4
         CH    R7,=H'8'      LONGER THAN 8 CHARS?
         BH    BADLOC        THAT'S NO GOOD
         LA    R3,CLCBUF     ADDRESS TO COPY STRING TO
         MVC   CLCBUF,=CL8' ' CLEAR IT FIRST
         BCTR  R7,0          -1 FOR EXECUTE
         EX    R7,COPY       COPY THE STRING
         TR    CLCBUF,UPCASE UPPER CASE IT
         CLC   CLCBUF,MAILUSER  THESE BETTER MATCH!!
         BNE   BADLOC        NAUGHTY USER!
         ICM   R7,B'1111',MBXDML GET HOST NAME NODE
         USING NODE,R7     ADDRESS IT                             EAC
         BNZ   HOSTOK        HOST LIST OK                           EAC
*-------- HOST NAME OMMITTED.  FILL IN LOCAL NODE NAME AS HOST NAME.EAC
*-------- BUILD A DUMMY NODE->TOKEND->CPUSTR                      EAC
         LA    R1,FAKENODE   DUMMY NODE                           EAC
         ST    R1,MBXDML         STUFF INTO MBOX                 EAC
         MVC   MBXDCNT,=F'1' SET LENGTH 1                           EAC
         LR    R7,R1         FIX UP NODE BASE                     EAC
         LA    R1,CPUSTR     LOCAL MACHINE NAME                     EAC
         ST    R1,FAKETOK+(TOKPTR-TOKEND) SET TOKEN POINTER
         LA    R1,CPUSTR+8                                          EAC
         MVI   TRAPTAB+C' ',X'FF'                                   EAC
         TRT   CPUSTR,TRAPTAB FIND LENGTH OF STRING                 EAC
         MVI   TRAPTAB+C' ',X'00'                                   EAC
         LA    R0,CPUSTR                                            EAC
         SR    R1,R0         LENGTH OF STRING                       EAC
         ST    R1,FAKETOK+(TOKLEN-TOKEND)
*-------- CHAIN FAKE "AT HOST" ONTO SENDER FIELDD AND SET EDIT FLAG EAC
         LA    R1,FITOK      GET LIST OF TOKENS                     EAC
FINDEND  EQU   *                                                    EAC
         ICM   R2,B'1111',0(R1) GET POINTER TO NEXT ONE             EAC
         BZ    FOUNDEND      FOUND END OF LIST                      EAC
         USING TOKEND,R2
         CLI   TOKTYPE,TOKRTB   RIGHT BRACE
         BE    FOUNDEND
         LR    R1,R2         CHAIN ALONG                            EAC
         B     FINDEND                                              EAC
FOUNDEND EQU   *                                                    EAC
***********************************************************************
*                                                                     *
* NOTE:  The following code should be changed to build the TOKEND     *
*        on the stack (and do 2 way chaining).  This is left as a     *
*        future project.                                              *
*                                                                     *
***********************************************************************
         LA    R0,FAKETOK0   ADD INTO CHAIN
         STCM  R0,B'0111',1(R1)
         ST    R2,FAKETOK+TOKNEXT-TOKEND
         OI    FIFLG1,FIEDIFLG
HOSTOK   EQU   *                                                    EAC
         ST    R7,NODEP            Set NODE pointer for GENLIST.
         MVC   STKP,=A(LCLSTACK)   Init stack pointer
         MVC   STKL,=A(L'LCLSTACK)    and length.
         CALL  GENLIST,(NODEP,DOMA,DOML,STKP,STKL) Build HOST string.
         LTR   R15,R15             Did it work?
         BNZ   BADLOC              No  : Fail the message.
         L     R2,DOMA             Get string address
         L     R7,DOML                and length.
         DROP  R5,R7
*----------------------------------------------------------------[1.22]
* If any RSCS-domains are defined and the hostname ends in one, then
* strip it off since the various tables don't include them.
*----------------------------------------------------------------[1.22]
         LA    R14,L'RSCSDOM/4     Number of RSCS-Domains.
         LA    R15,RSCSDOM         First RSCS-Domain.
DOMLOOP0 DS    0H
         ICM   R4,B'1111',0(R15) no RSCS domain string defined?
         BZ    NORSCSD       so stop wasting time!               [1.22]
         SR    R5,R5         get a zero                          [1.22]
         IC    R5,0(R4)      get length of domain string         [1.22]
         LR    R3,R5         make a copy for later               [1.22]
         LR    R1,R7         length of token                     [1.22]
         SR    R1,R5         minus length of domain string       [1.22]
         BM    DOMNEXT       token too short to include it       [1.22]
         LA    R1,0(R1,R2)   beginning of possible match         [1.22]
         LA    R4,1(R4)      beginning of domain string          [1.22]
         SR    R0,R0         0 will contain one character        [1.22]
         SR    R6,R6         and 6 the other                     [1.22]
DOMLOOP  EQU   *             loop to compare token end to domain [1.22]
         IC    R0,0(R1)      get next token character            [1.22]
         O     R0,=X'00000040' upper case it                     [1.22]
         IC    R6,0(R4)      get next domain string character    [1.22]
         O     R6,=X'00000040' upper case it too                 [1.22]
         CR    R0,R6         compare the upper case characters   [1.22]
         BNE   DOMNEXT       don't match; exit loop
         LA    R1,1(R1)      increment pointer                   [1.22]
         LA    R4,1(R4)      ditto for domain string             [1.22]
         BCT   R5,DOMLOOP    loop for length of string           [1.22]
* falling thru here means they match.                            [1.22]
         SR    R7,R3         chop off end of string              [1.22]
         B     DOMDONE
DOMNEXT  DS    0H
         LA    R15,4(,R15)         Try the next RSCS-Domain
         BCT   R14,DOMLOOP0           if there is one.
NORSCSD  EQU   *             no rscs domain given                [1.22]
DOMDONE  EQU   *             fall thru here to old lookup code   [1.22]
         L     R3,MAILRTAB   LOOK IN ROUTING TABLE FOR AN ALIAS
         CALL  TBLUK,((R3),(R2),(R7),TWORK)
         LTR   R15,R15       FIND IT?
         BNZ   TRYLDOM             No  : Try LocalDomain.
         USING ROUTD,R1      ADDRESS THE ENTRY
         CLC   RTROUTE,CPUSTR IS IT AN ALIAS FOR THIS NODE?
         DROP  R1
         BNE   TRYLDOM       Nope
         SR    R15,R15       OK RETCODE
         B     RET
         SPACE ,
TRYLDOM  DS    0H
         LA    R15,LCLHOST         Address of LocalDomain array.
         LA    R14,L'LCLHOST/4     Number of entries in LCLHOST.
TLDLOOP  DS    0H
         ICM   R3,B'1111',0(R15)   Is there a LocalDomain?
         BZ    BADLOC              No  : Bad address.
         SR    R1,R1               Get Local-Domain
         IC    R1,0(,R3)              length.
         CR    R7,R1               Do the lengths match?
         BNE   TLDNEXT             No  : Bad address.
         BCTR  R1,0
         EX    R1,TLD$CLC          "CLC 0(*-*,R2),1(R3)"
         BE    TLDGOOD             Yes : Accept it.
TLDNEXT  DS    0H
         LA    R15,4(,R15)         Update pointer
         BCT   R14,TLDLOOP            and loop.
         B     BADLOC              End of list : Bad address.
TLDGOOD  DS    0H
         SR    R15,R15             Yes : Accept <user>@<lcldom>.
         B     RET
TLD$CLC  CLC   0(*-*,R2),1(R3)     *** Executed ***
         SPACE ,
*----------------------------------------------------------------[1.23]
*     Get here if we trust the sender because he is in table     [1.23]
*     but has no exit to call or because his exit says he's OK.  [1.23]
*----------------------------------------------------------------[1.23]
VALTRUST EQU   *                                                 [1.23]
**--- DO SOME STATISTICS
         USING VALD,R8       address the vald                    [1.23]
         L     R1,VAMSGCNT   GET MSG COUNTER
         LA    R1,1(R1)      BUMP SUCCESS COUNTER
         ST    R1,VAMSGCNT   STUFF IT BACK
         LA    R1,MAILSFB    GET SFB
         USING SFBLOK,R1     ADDRESS
         L     R1,SFBRECNO   GET NUMBER OF RECORDS IN FILE
         DROP  R1
         C     R1,VAMSGMAX   BIGGER THAN MAXIMUM?
         BL    NOTMAX        NOT THE NEW MAX THEN
         ST    R1,VAMSGMAX   SET NEW MAXIMUM
NOTMAX   EQU   *
         A     R1,VAMSGLEN   ADD TO LENGTH TOTAL
         ST    R1,VAMSGLEN   THIS IS NEW TOTAL
         DROP  R8
         SR    R15,R15       RETURN OK
RET      EQU   *
         LTR   R15,R15       some validation error               [1.23]
         BZ    RET1          nope                                [1.23]
         OI    MAILFLG2,MFLG2VLF VaLidate Failed                 [1.23]
RET1     EQU   *                                                 [1.23]
         L     R13,4(R13)              GET CALLER'S SAVE PTR
         L     R14,12(R13)             GET R14
         LM    R0,R12,20(R13)          GET R0-R12
         BR    R14                     RETURN
         SPACE ,
*--------------------------------------------------------------------
*        ERROR EXITS
*--------------------------------------------------------------------
NOSNDR   EQU   *             DIDN'T GIVE FROM OR SENDER
         WTR   VAL020
         LA    R15,4
         B     RET
         SPACE ,
BADLOC   EQU   *             LOCAL USER GAVE BAD ADDRESS
         WTR   VAL021
         LA    R15,4
         B     RET
         SPACE ,
*----------------------------------------------------------------[1.23]
*    Get here if sender is not in the table and file is from     [1.23]
*    the network.  Check to see if sending userid is a generic
*    id (identified as '*DEFAULT* userid' in the INCOMING table.
*
*    If a generic id is not found, check to see if Allow-Unknown-Nodes
*    is true and try the *DEFAULT* entry in the table before giving up
*    on him.                                                     [1.23]
*----------------------------------------------------------------[1.23]
NETWORK  EQU   *             UNKNOWN NETWORK SENDER              [1.23]
         MVC   GENERICU,MAILUSER       Source user
         CALL  TBLUK,((R5),GENERIC,L'GENERIC,TWORK)
         LR    R8,R1         Get a better handle
         LTR   R15,R15       Found it?
         BZ    DEFAUN        Do default unknown node processing
         SPACE 1
*  SEE IF THE ALLOW-UNKNOWN-NODES FLAG IS ON. IF SO, IGNORE THIS
*  ERROR.
         TM    MAILOPTS,MOPTAUN        CHECK FLAG
         BNO   BADNET1       IT'S OFF, DON'T LET THE FILE IN
         CALL  TBLUK,((R5),DEFAULT,L'DEFAULT,TWORK)
         LR    R8,R1         GET A BETTER HANDLE
         LTR   R15,R15       FOUND IT?
         BZ    DEFAUN        DO DEFAULT UNKNOWN NODE PROCESSING
         SR    R15,R15       ALLOW IT WITH NO VALIDITY CHECKER
         B     RET           CLEAN EXIT
BADNET1  EQU   *
         LA    R4,MAILNODE   NODE NAME
         LA    R5,MAILUSER   USER ID
         WTR   VAL019,(CA,(R4),CA,(R5))
         LA    R15,4
         B     RET
DEFAUN   EQU   *                      here if MOPTAUN works      [1.23]
         USING VALD,R8                look at the VALD           [1.23]
         ICM   R15,B'1111',VAADDR     user exit supplied?        [1.23]
         DROP  R8                     done w/vald                [1.23]
         BZ    VALTRUST               no; trust the sender       [1.23]
         ST    R11,USERVPAR           set up exit plist          [1.23]
         ST    R8,USERVPAR+4          "                          [1.23]
         LA    R1,USERVPAR            point to PLIST             [1.23]
         BALR  R14,R15                call it                    [1.23]
         LTR   R15,R15                did they like him?         [1.23]
         BZ    VALTRUST               yes; trust the sender      [1.23]
*      fall thru here;  don't trust him                          [1.23]
*----------------------------------------------------------------[1.23]
*    Get here if sender is in table and his user exit doesn't    [1.23]
*    like him.                                                   [1.23]
*----------------------------------------------------------------[1.23]
VALFAIL  EQU   *             USER VALIDATION FAILED
         USING VALD,R8
         L     R1,VAMSGFAI   GET FAILURE COUNT
         LA    R1,1(R1)      UP IT ONE
         ST    R1,VAMSGFAI   AND PUT BACK INTO FAILURE COUNT
         DROP  R8
         LR    R5,R15        GET RC
         WTR   VAL024        ISSUE MESSAGE
         LA    R15,4         MINOR ERROR
         B     RET           GO DIE
         SPACE ,
NOSPACE  EQU   *
         WTR   VAL003,(CA,MYNAME)
         LA    R15,8
         BR    R14
         SPACE ,
NODATE   EQU   *             NO DATE SUPPLIED
         WTR   VAL023        ISSUE THE MESSAGE
         LA    R15,4         RETURN MINOR ERROR
         B     RET           AND RETURN
         SPACE ,
RSCSREJ  EQU   *
         LA    R15,4         ERROR RETURN
         B     RET
         SPACE
HOPCOUNT EQU   *             <- too many received: lines         [1.24]
         WTR   VAL063        write error message                 [1.24]
         LA    R15,4         return minor error                  [1.24]
         B     RET           -> and return                       [1.24]
         SPACE ,                                                 [1.24]
*begin [1.18]-----
*        ALWAYS send xfer'd mail to the maintainer.  It would
*        certainly confuse the originator to get the error mail
*        because one of his recipients was dumb enough to transfer
*        the file back to mailer.
*-------------------------------------------------------------------
BADXFER  EQU   *
BADUXFER EQU   *                       <- so I'm lazy...         [1.24]
         NI    MAILFLG1,X'FF'-MFLG1HDS say header was invalid (lie)
         MVC   MAILUSER,MAINTID        always send to maintainer
         MVC   MAILNODE,MAINTNOD       ...
         MVC   MAILULEN,=F'8'      Fix up the length for MAILRET.
         MVC   MAILNLEN,=F'8'      Fix up the length for MAILRET.
         WTR   VAL048
         LA    R15,4
         B     RET
*end [1.18]-------
         EJECT ,
*--------------------------------------------------------------------
*        ROUTINES TO SUPPLY DEFAULT VALUES FOR DATE AND SENDER
*        FIELDS OF THE HEADER.  THESE ROUTINES ARE INVOKED IF
*        THE INCOMING MAIL FILE WAS LACKING THE FIELD AND THE
*        SUPPLY-MISSING-FIELDS FLAG WAS TRUE.
*        A FIELDD, TOKEND AND TEXT STRINGS ARE ALLOCATTED ON THE
*        STACK FOR THESE FIELDS AND TBADD IS CALLED TO ADD THEM
*        TO THE MAILKTAB.
*--------------------------------------------------------------------
         SPACE ,
FILLDATE EQU   *
         BR    R14
         SPACE ,
FILLSEND EQU   *
         BR    R14
         SPACE ,
COPY     MVC   0(0,R3),0(R2)
         LTORG ,
SENDER   DC    C'SENDER'
FROM     DC    C'FROM'
DATE     DC    C'DATE'
RSENDER  DC    C'RESENT-SENDER'        [1.16]
RFROM    DC    C'RESENT-FROM'          [1.16]
RDATE    DC    C'RESENT-DATE'          [1.16]
         SPACE 1
GENERIC  DS    0CL16
         DC    CL8'*DEFAULT*'
GENERICU DC    CL8'userid   '          Replaced with sender's id
         SPACE 1
DEFAULT  DC    0CL16' ',CL8'*DEFAULT*',CL8'*DEFAULT*'
SAVE     DS    18F                     SAVE AREA
TWORK    DS    64F
ADSTR    DS    2F
ADSTK    DS    2F
TOKLIST  DS    F
PARSLIST DS    F
USERVPAR DS    A             USER EXIT PARM LIST
NETNODE  DC    CL16' '
CLCBUF   DS    CL8
         DS    0D
FAKENODE DC    (NODSIZ)X'0'
         ORG   FAKENODE
         DC    F'0'          NODNEXT is zero
         DC    F'0'          NODPREV is zero
         DC    A(FAKETOK)    POINT TO DUMMY TOKEND
         SPACE 1
FAKETOK  DS    (TOKSIZ)X'0'
         ORG   FAKETOK
         DC    A(0)          No next token
         DC    A(0)          No previous token
         DC    A(0)          No string pointer
         DC    F'0'          Length of zero
         DC    AL1(TOKATM)   Atom type token
         ORG   ,
         SPACE 1
FAKETOK0 DS    (TOKSIZ)X'0'
         ORG   FAKETOK0
         DC    A(FAKETOK)    Next token
         DC    A(0)          No previous token
         DC    A(ATSIGN)     String pointer
         DC    F'1'          String length
         DC    AL1(TOKAT)    Token is at sign
         ORG   ,
         SPACE 1
ATSIGN   DC    CL1'@'                                      [1.16]
DOMA     DS    A                   Address of host string.
DOML     DS    F                   Length of host string.
STKP     DS    A                   Stack Pointer.
STKL     DS    F                   Stack Length.
NODEP    DS    A                   Address of NODE for GENLIST.
LCLSTACK DS    XL100               Local stack area.
         END   VALIDATE
